   "Statement": "<b>Occupation</b><br>Judge Pro Tempore, Thurston County District Court, Olympia Municipal Court; Pierce County Deputy Prosecuting Attorney<br><br><b>Education</b><br>BA, Pacific Lutheran University; JD, Willamette University College of Law<br><br><b>Statement</b><br>Sven Nelson has dedicated his career to serving Pierce County. As a <em>Deputy Prosecuting Attorney</em>, he's tried serious felonies involving sexual assault, elder abuse, and homicide. He served as a <em>Judge Pro Tempore</em>, earning a reputation for integrity, fairness, and knowledge of the law. His experience on both sides of the bench provides a practical understanding of how a judge's decisions affect victims, defendants, and families.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">For a decade, he led <em>Pierce County's Elder Abuse Multidisciplinary Team</em>, coordinating law enforcement, prosecutors, and social services to better protect vulnerable adults. Beyond the courtroom, he's an elected Trustee of the <em>Tacoma-Pierce County Bar Association</em> and former Board President of <em>Rebuilding Hope Sexual Assault Center</em>.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><em>Endorsements:</em> Retiring Pos. 8 Judge Lineberry, a majority of Pierce County's District Court and Superior Court judges, Former County Executive Ladenburg, Former County Executive Dammeier, County Executive Mello, and Tacoma Mayor Ibsen. <em>Please vote Sven Nelson for Judge.</em></p><div><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">&nbsp;</p></div><p> ",
