   "Statement": "<strong>Occupation</strong><br>Attorney, Municipal Court Judge Pro Tem, District Court Judge Pro Tem&nbsp;</p><p class=\"InDesignStatementheader\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><br><strong>Education</strong><br>JD: Seattle University School of Law, BA:&nbsp;Western Washington University</p><p class=\"InDesignStatementheader\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><br><br><strong>Statement</strong><br>As a proud United States Marine Corps veteran, I learned that leadership requires discipline, integrity, and duty. I have carried these values throughout my 26-year legal career as a veteran trial attorney, Judge Pro Tempore, and Presiding Judge. I will bring that leadership to the Pierce County District Court to command a fair, orderly, and efficient courtroom.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">As the Presiding Judge at Bremerton Municipal Court, I exercised full responsibility for the court’s budget, personnel, and day-to-day operations. I made the tough decisions necessary to restructure staff, restore public trust, and streamline processes. I know exactly how to manage high-volume criminal dockets, preside over complex jury trials, and issue fair, well-reasoned decisions grounded in law and evidence.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">I ask for your vote to bring this proven experience to the Pierce County District Court bench. I would be honored to have your support to deliver real, community-changing results. Thank you.</p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"></p><p> ",
